eDNAFlow LCA standalone adaptation

This repository contains a modified derivative of the Lowest Common Ancestor
(LCA) taxonomy-assignment component from eDNAFlow by Mahsa
Mousavi-Derazmahalleh and contributors:
https://github.com/mahsa-mousavi/eDNAFlow

Original publication:
Mousavi-Derazmahalleh M, Stott A, Lines R, Peverley G, Nester G, Simpson T,
Zawierta M, De La Pierre M, Bunce M, Christophersen CT (2021). eDNAFlow, an
automated, reproducible and scalable workflow for analysis of environmental
DNA sequences exploiting Nextflow and Singularity. Molecular Ecology
Resources 21:1697-1704. DOI: 10.1111/1755-0998.13356.

Upstream provenance retained for audit:
- upstream_runAssign_collapsedTaxonomy.py corresponds to upstream eDNAFlow
  history at commit 0c88d6f ("filter general uncultured stuff").
- upstream_working_function.py corresponds to upstream eDNAFlow history at
  commit ec94ab1.

The retained files may differ byte-for-byte from GitHub's historical blobs due
to line-ending normalisation; the provenance statement concerns source content
and upstream history rather than byte identity.

Modified for standalone packaging and Galaxy use by Olly Berry, CSIRO.
Release-remediation and modification record updated: 2026-11-09.

CSIRO modifications for this standalone adaptation include, at a high level:
- removal of runtime shell-based taxonomy download and fixed intermediate files;
- a packaged command-line interface with explicit inputs and outputs;
- literal 22-column eDNAFlow BLAST parsing and input validation;
- stable per-feature hit evaluation so interleaved features cannot change
  another feature's adjacent-hit filtering result;
- independently reviewed compatibility tests and documented corrections to
  numeric identity-difference and cross-domain LCA behaviour;
- rank-aware NCBI taxonomy using rankedlineage.dmp plus nodes.dmp, including
  consistency checks when nodes.dmp is explicitly supplied;
- preservation of blank domain semantics rather than relabelling kingdom as
  domain;
- per-hit taxon-name, taxon-rank and lineage provenance;
- a Galaxy wrapper with managed and custom taxonomy routes;
- a versioned Galaxy Data Manager with persistent reference registration,
  independent checksums, structural validation and a finite download timeout;
- Python packaging, automated tests and a Bioconda recipe.

The differential-review harness under review-tools/ was developed during an
independent AI-assisted review and then used and extended during release
remediation. Its named cases and executable checks are retained as audit and
regression evidence; generated scratch outputs are not release specifications.

